Use Optional, or check for null explicitly before the call.

Example:
// Wrong
return user.getName();

// Right
return Optional.ofNullable(user).map(User::getName).orElse("Unknown");

Use a PreparedStatement, or the parameter binding provided by your ORM.

Example:
// Wrong
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '" + name + "'";

// Right
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?";

Use try-with-resources so the resource is closed automatically.

Example:
// Right
try (FileInputStream fis = new FileInputStream("file.txt")) {
    // read the file
}

Use ConcurrentHashMap in multi-threaded code.

Example:
Map<String, String> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
